    "text": "To determine how much money Mica should have to buy all the items, we need to calculate the cost of each item and then sum these costs.\n\n1. **Cost of pasta:**\n   Mica bought 2 kilograms of pasta, and the cost is $1.5 per kilogram.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of pasta} = 2 \\times 1.5 = 3 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Cost of ground beef:**\n   Mica bought \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) kilogram of ground beef, and the cost is $8 per kilogram.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of ground beef} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 = 2 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Cost of pasta sauce:**\n   Mica bought two jars of pasta sauce, and each jar costs $2.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of pasta sauce} = 2 \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Cost of Quesadilla:**\n   Mica wants to buy a $6 Quesadilla.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of Quesadilla} = 6 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum the costs of all the items to find the total amount of money Mica needs.\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = 3 + 2 + 4 + 6 = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the amount of money Mica should have with her to buy all those items is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).",
